.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH git-veil-tell 1  "git-veil-tell " 
.SH NAME
git\-veil\-tell \- Add a collaborator\*(Aqs public key to the keyring and re\-sign it
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBgit\-veil tell\fR [\fB\-\-remote\fR] [\fB\-\-key\-store\fR] [\fB\-\-passphrase\-stdin\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIEMAIL\fR> <\fIPUBLIC_KEY\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Add a collaborator\*(Aqs public key to the keyring and re\-sign it
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-remote\fR \fI<REMOTE>\fR [default: origin]
Git remote name
.TP
\fB\-\-key\-store\fR \fI<KEY_STORE>\fR
Key store directory (default: $HOME/.git\-veil)
.TP
\fB\-\-passphrase\-stdin\fR
Read the passphrase for a passphrase\-protected private key from stdin (exactly one line). Wins over the GITVEIL_PASSPHRASE environment variable; never pass a passphrase as a CLI argument
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
<\fIEMAIL\fR>
Collaborator\*(Aqs email
.TP
<\fIPUBLIC_KEY\fR>
Path to collaborator\*(Aqs public key file
.SH EXTRA
Adds a collaborator\*(Aqs public key to the repository keyring and re\-signs
the keyring with the owner\*(Aqs private key. The existing keyring signature
is verified against the pinned trusted key before any modification, and a
canary is test\-encrypted to the new key so a key that cannot encrypt is
never signed into the ring.

Requires init, an established trust pin (trust) for this repository on
this machine, and the owner\*(Aqs private key in the local key store
(import). Next steps: add files, then hide.

EXAMPLES
  $ git\-veil tell alice@example.com alice.pub
  $ git\-veil tell alice@example.com alice.pub \-\-passphrase\-stdin < pass.txt
